*
* START-HISTORY:
* 25 Oct 26 Windows port - from Linux 04f1eaa - the screen library as of S.75 TK-0.13 (containers and viewports, slider, selector, colour, accelerators, table styles)
* 12 Oct 26 dm  New.
* 13 Oct 26 dm  Sorting, row marks (multi), horizontal scrolling by column, column width changes.
* 18 Oct 26 dm  The cursor is placed through $sl_curat (which tells the cursor lock where it is).
* 22 Oct 26 dm  S.75 TK-0.5 (G3): rowstyle (a style for a row), the K column (a check cell), filter (the rows that hold a text) and the refresh op (new rows, the
*               current row, the sort and the marks kept by a key column).  n is now the number of rows SHOWN and nr the number there are; the sort and the filter
*               are one subroutine, order.rows.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $sl_table(op, w, scr, key, ret)      the widget contract; w is a collection (see $sl_label)
*
*   Elements:  id, ax ay (the top left cell on the screen), w h (the whole widget: the heading row, then
*   h - 1 rows of data, and in the last column of the widget a scroll bar), cols (the columns, as values: the
*   heading, and as a subvalue what it is to look like - a width and then L, R or C for left, right or centred,
*   '20L' or '6R'; a column given no width is as wide as its heading and the widest cell among its first 200 rows, at
*   most 30), rows (the data: one row to a field, one cell to a value), multi (1: rows can be marked), cur (the
*   current row, 1 to start with: its place on the screen), top (the first row shown), value (the number of the
*   current row in rows - or with multi the numbers of the rows marked, as values), and the state: ord (the numbers of
*   the rows in the order shown, null when it is the order of rows), ccol (the current column), hcol (the first column
*   shown), sortcol and sortdir (the column the rows are sorted by, and 1 up or 2 down), cwid (a width a column was
*   given by the keys, as values, 0 for none), picked (the numbers of the rows marked, as values)
*
*     init    the columns' widths; w and h from the columns and the rows if they were not given (the heading and at most
*             8 rows); cur and top are brought into range; the order is that of rows
*     draw    the heading in the 'header' style, then the rows in the 'text' style, one column apart; the current
*             row is in the highlight style while the table has the focus and marked with > while it has not (with
*             marker 1 - an element a caller sets, as CED does - it is marked with > in both cases); with multi
*             a row that is marked has a * in front of it.  The current column's heading is in the highlight style
*             while the table has the focus (when there is more than one column) and the sorted column's has a ^ or v
*             in its last cell.  A table wider than the widget shows the columns from hcol on and a row longer than that
*             is cut at the right-hand edge
*     focus   key = 1 gives it the focus (draws), key = 0 takes it away (draws)
*     key     up, down, home, end, pgup, pgdn move among the rows; left and right move among the columns (the table
*             scrolls sideways to show the current one; at the first or last column they are 'unhandled'); a letter jumps
*             to the next row whose first cell starts with it; f3 sorts by the current column - up, then down, then the
*             order of rows again (numbers by value, other text without regard to case); < and > make the current
*             column narrower or wider; with multi the space bar marks or unmarks the current row.  ret<1> is 'handled';
*             (22 Oct 26, G3: the elements below are set by the program that owns the table; the table never changes them.)
*             rowstyle: values, one for each row of rows (its number in rows, not its place on the screen): the name of a theme style ('disabled', 'error',
*             'todo' ...) the row is drawn in when it is not the current row of a table that has the focus; null for the text style.
*             A column given the letter K (as in '5K'; width 3 or the heading, whichever is wider, when no width is given) is a check cell: a cell holding a non-zero
*             number is drawn [x], any other [ ].  The cells are not changed.
*             filter: a text.  Only the rows that hold it in some cell, without regard to case, are shown, in the sort order; the current row stays if it still
*             matches, else it is the first.  After the program changes filter it calls op 'filter'.  Marks on rows the filter hides are KEPT, so Return (multi) can
*             answer rows that are not on the screen: a program that acts on them says so (nshown, below, is how many are shown).
*             keycol: the number of a column whose cells are unique keys.  Op 'refresh' takes the new rows from the element newrows (and empties it), shows them in the
*             sort and filter in force, and keeps the current row, the marks and the place of the current row in the window BY THE KEY (a current row that is gone
*             falls to the same place, or the last row).  Without keycol, marks are dropped and the current row is kept by place.  The op ret is 'handled'.
*             nshown (set by every op): the number of rows shown.  ret<1> is 'handled';
*             'done' (Return, ret<2> the number of the current row, or with multi the numbers of those marked); 'cancel'
*             (Esc); or 'unhandled' with ret<2> the key's name (tab, btab, a function key; and up on the first row, down
*             on the last, left and right at the ends, so that a form can go on to the widget before or after)
*     mouse   a click on a row makes it current (with multi it also marks or unmarks it); a second click on the same row
*             is Return; a click on a heading makes that column current and sorts by it (as f3); the wheel moves three rows
*     close   nothing to undo
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine sl_table(op, w, scr, key, ret)
$catalog $sl_table

$include sl.h

   ret = ''
   cols = w{'cols'}
   nc = dcount(cols, @vm)
   if cols = '' then nc = 0
   rows = w{'rows'}
   nr = dcount(rows, @fm)                            ;* the rows there are
   if rows = '' then nr = 0
   cur = w{'cur'} + 0
   top = w{'top'} + 0
   multi = w{'multi'} + 0
   ord = w{'ord'}
   filter = w{'filter'}
   fon = w{'fon'} + 0                                ;* 1 when the order in ord was made with a filter (then ord is the rows shown, even when it is empty)
   rowstyle = w{'rowstyle'}
   n = nr                                            ;* the rows SHOWN
   if ord # '' or fon then n = dcount(ord, @vm)
   if ord = '' then
      if fon then n = 0
   end
   picked = w{'picked'}
   ccol = w{'ccol'} + 0
   hcol = w{'hcol'} + 0
   sortcol = w{'sortcol'} + 0
   sortdir = w{'sortdir'} + 0
   cwid = w{'cwid'}
   colsel = w{'colsel'} + 0                          ;* 1 once a key or click has used the columns: then the current one shows

   begin case
      case op = 'init'
         w{'type'} = 'table'
         w{'focusable'} = 1
         ord = '' ; picked = '' ; cwid = '' ; ccol = 1 ; hcol = 1 ; sortcol = 0 ; sortdir = 0 ; colsel = 0 ; fon = 0
         gosub widths
         gosub order.rows                         ;* a filter the program set before init shows from the start
         if w{'w'} = '' or w{'w'} + 0 < 4 then w{'w'} = tot + 1       ;* the cells, and the scroll bar column
         if w{'h'} = '' or w{'h'} + 0 < 2 then
            bh = n
            if bh > 8 then bh = 8
            if bh < 1 then bh = 1
            w{'h'} = bh + 1
         end
         if cur < 1 or cur > n then cur = 1
         if n = 0 then cur = 0
         top = 1
         th = w{'h'} + 0 - 1                      ;* the rows of data shown
         gosub scroll
         gosub store

      case op = 'draw'
         gosub widths
         th = w{'h'} + 0 - 1
         gosub paint

      case op = 'focus'
         w{'focused'} = if key then 1 else 0
         gosub widths
         th = w{'h'} + 0 - 1
         gosub paint

      case op = 'key'
         w{'clk'} = ''
         gosub widths
         th = w{'h'} + 0 - 1
         gosub handle.key

      case op = 'mouse'
         gosub widths
         th = w{'h'} + 0 - 1
         gosub click

      case op = 'filter'                         ;* the program changed the element filter
         gosub widths
         th = w{'h'} + 0 - 1
         gosub do.filter
         ret = 'handled'

      case op = 'refresh'                        ;* the program put new rows in the element newrows
         gosub do.refresh
         ret = 'handled'
   end case

   return

* The element filter has changed: the order is made again and the current row stays if it is still shown, else it is the first
do.filter:
   keep = 0
   if cur >= 1 and cur <= n then
      i = cur
      gosub orig
      keep = oi
   end
   gosub order.rows
   cur = 1
   if keep then
      for r = 1 to n
         i = r
         gosub orig
         if oi = keep then cur = r ; exit
      next r
   end
   if n = 0 then cur = 0
   top = 1
   gosub scroll
   gosub store
   gosub paint
   return

* New rows in newrows.  With a key column (keycol) the current row, the marks and the current row's place in the window are kept by the key; the sort and
* the filter in force are applied to the new rows.  Without one the marks go and the current row stays at its place (or the last row).
do.refresh:
   keycol = w{'keycol'} + 0
   ck = ''
   pk = ''
   if keycol > 0 then
      if cur >= 1 and cur <= n then
         i = cur
         gosub orig
         ck = rows<oi, keycol>
      end
      np = dcount(picked, @vm)
      if picked = '' then np = 0
      for k = 1 to np
         pk<1, -1> = rows<picked<1, k>, keycol>
      next k
   end
   off = cur - top
   if off < 0 then off = 0
   rows = w{'newrows'}
   w{'rows'} = rows
   w{'newrows'} = ''
   nr = dcount(rows, @fm)
   if rows = '' then nr = 0
   gosub widths
   th = w{'h'} + 0 - 1
   gosub order.rows
   newcur = 0
   if ck # '' then
      for r = 1 to n
         i = r
         gosub orig
         if rows<oi, keycol> = ck then newcur = r ; exit
      next r
   end
   if newcur = 0 then
      newcur = cur                                   ;* the current row is gone (or there is no key): the same place, or the last row
      if newcur > n then newcur = n
      if newcur < 1 and n > 0 then newcur = 1
   end
   cur = newcur
   if n = 0 then cur = 0
   picked = ''
   if keycol > 0 and pk # '' then
      for r = 1 to nr
         v = rows<r, keycol>
         locate v in pk<1, 1> setting at then picked<1, -1> = r
      next r
   end
   top = cur - off                                   ;* the current row keeps its place in the window ...
   if top > n - th + 1 then top = n - th + 1         ;* ... unless that would leave the window part empty when the rows could fill it
   if top < 1 then top = 1
   gosub scroll
   gosub store
   if not(w{'nopaint'} + 0) then gosub paint         ;* screen_set draws the whole form itself
   return

* The number in rows of the row shown at place i
orig:
   oi = i
   if ord # '' then oi = ord<1, i>
   return

* A click on a row makes it the current one (with multi it is also marked or unmarked); a second click on the row the
* last click chose is Return.  A click on the heading makes that column current and sorts by it; below the last row it
* does nothing.  The wheel moves the current row three at a time.
click:
   ret = 'handled'
   if key<1> = 'wheel' then
      if key<2> = 'up' then cur -= 3 else cur += 3
      if cur > n then cur = n
      if cur < 1 and n > 0 then cur = 1
   end else
      if key<4> = w{'ay'} then
         * the heading: the column under the click
         x = 1
         hit = 0
         for c = hcol to nc
            if key<3> - w{'ax'} >= x and key<3> - w{'ax'} < x + cw<1, c> then hit = c ; exit
            x += cw<1, c> + 1
         next c
         w{'clk'} = ''                              ;* a click on a heading is not the first half of a double click
         if hit then
            ccol = hit
            colsel = 1
            gosub sort.column
            cur = 1
         end
      end else
         i = top + key<4> - w{'ay'} - 1
         if i < 1 or i > n then return
         if i = w{'clk'} then
            gosub answer
            ret = 'done' : @fm : answer
            return
         end
         cur = i
         w{'clk'} = i
         if multi then
            gosub orig
            gosub toggle.mark
         end
      end
   end
   gosub scroll
   gosub store
   gosub paint
   return

* answer = what Return gives: the number of the current row, or with multi the numbers of those marked (the current one
* if none is)
answer:
   i = cur
   gosub orig
   answer = oi
   if multi and picked # '' then answer = picked
   return

* The row oi (its number in rows) is marked or not
toggle.mark:
   at = 0
   np = dcount(picked, @vm)
   if picked = '' then np = 0
   for k = 1 to np
      if picked<1, k> = oi then at = k ; exit
   next k
   if at then
      del picked<1, at>
   end else
      picked<1, -1> = oi
   end
   return

* cw = the width of each column (values), ca = how each is aligned, tot = the width of all of them with the gaps
widths:
   cw = ''
   ca = ''
   tot = 1                                           ;* the cell before the first column marks the current row
   for c = 1 to nc
      hd = cols<1, c, 1>
      sp = upcase(cols<1, c, 2>)
      al = 'L'
      if sp # '' then
         lst = sp[len(sp), 1]
         if lst = 'L' or lst = 'R' or lst = 'C' or lst = 'K' then
            al = lst
            sp = sp[1, len(sp) - 1]
         end
      end
      wd = sp + 0
      if wd < 1 and al = 'K' then
         wd = len(hd)                                ;* a check cell is [x]: three cells at least
         if wd < 3 then wd = 3
      end
      if wd < 1 then
         wd = len(hd)
         m = nr
         if m > 200 then m = 200
         for r = 1 to m
            if len(rows<r, c>) > wd then wd = len(rows<r, c>)
         next r
         if wd > 30 then wd = 30
         if wd < 1 then wd = 1
      end
      if cwid<1, c> + 0 > 0 then wd = cwid<1, c> + 0   ;* a width the keys gave it
      cw<1, c> = wd
      ca<1, c> = al
      tot += wd + 1
   next c
   if tot > 1 then tot -= 1
   return

handle.key:
   ret = 'handled'
   if key = 'left' or key = 'right' or key = 'f3' or key = '<' or key = '>' then colsel = 1
   begin case
      case key = 'esc'
         ret = 'cancel'
      case key = 'enter'
         gosub answer
         ret = 'done' : @fm : answer
      case key = 'down'
         if cur < n then cur += 1 else ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : key
      case key = 'up'
         if cur > 1 then cur -= 1 else ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : key
      case key = 'left'
         if ccol > 1 then ccol -= 1 else ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : key
      case key = 'right'
         if ccol < nc then ccol += 1 else ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : key
      case key = 'home'
         if n > 0 then cur = 1
      case key = 'end'
         cur = n
      case key = 'pgdn'
         cur += th - 1
         if cur > n then cur = n
      case key = 'pgup'
         cur -= th - 1
         if cur < 1 then cur = 1
         if n = 0 then cur = 0
      case key = 'f3'
         gosub sort.column
      case key = '<' or key = '>'
         if ccol >= 1 and ccol <= nc then
            wd = cw<1, ccol> + 0
            if key = '>' then wd += 1 else wd -= 1
            if wd < 1 then wd = 1
            if wd > 60 then wd = 60
            cwid<1, ccol> = wd
         end
      case key = ' ' and multi
         if cur >= 1 then
            i = cur
            gosub orig
            gosub toggle.mark
         end
      case len(key) = 1
         uk = upcase(key)
         found = 0
         for k = 1 to n
            i = cur + k
            if i > n then i -= n
            gosub orig
            if upcase(rows<oi, 1>[1, 1]) = uk then found = i ; exit
         next k
         if found then cur = found
      case 1
         ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : key
   end case
   if n = 0 then cur = 0
   gosub widths
   gosub scroll
   gosub store
   gosub paint
   return

* Sort by column ccol: up, then down, then the order of rows again.  The current row stays the same row.
sort.column:
   if ccol < 1 or ccol > nc or n = 0 then return
   i = cur
   gosub orig
   keep = oi                                         ;* the number of the current row
   if sortcol = ccol then
      sortdir += 1
      if sortdir > 2 then sortdir = 0
   end else
      sortcol = ccol
      sortdir = 1
   end
   if sortdir = 0 then sortcol = 0
   gosub order.rows
   cur = 1
   for r = 1 to n
      i = r
      gosub orig
      if oi = keep then cur = r ; exit
   next r
   return

* ord = the numbers of the rows in the order shown: sorted by sortcol and sortdir (the order of rows when sortdir is 0), then only the rows the filter lets
* through.  n = how many are shown, fon = 1 when a filter made the order.
order.rows:
   ord = ''
   if sortdir > 0 and sortcol >= 1 and sortcol <= nc and nr > 0 then
      * numbers by value when every cell of the column is a number, else the text without regard to case
      isnum = @true
      for r = 1 to nr
         v = rows<r, sortcol>
         if v # '' and not(num(v)) then isnum = @false ; exit
      next r
      lb = 'AL'
      if isnum then lb = 'AR'
      skeys = ''
      order = ''
      for r = 1 to nr
         v = rows<r, sortcol>
         if not(isnum) then v = upcase(v)
         locate v in skeys<1> by lb setting pos then
            pos += 1
         end
         ins v before skeys<pos>
         ins r before order<pos>
      next r
      if sortdir = 1 then
         ord = convert(@fm, @vm, order)
      end else
         for r = nr to 1 step -1
            ord<1, -1> = order<r>
         next r
      end
   end
   fon = 0
   if filter # '' then
      fon = 1
      uf = upcase(filter)
      kept = ''
      m = nr
      if ord # '' then m = dcount(ord, @vm)
      for k = 1 to m
         r = k
         if ord # '' then r = ord<1, k>
         if index(upcase(rows<r>), uf, 1) then kept<1, -1> = r
      next k
      ord = kept
   end
   n = nr
   if ord # '' or fon then n = dcount(ord, @vm)
   if ord = '' and fon then n = 0
   return

* Keep the current row inside the rows shown, and the current column inside the columns shown
scroll:
   if th < 1 then th = 1
   if cur < top then top = cur
   if cur > top + th - 1 then top = cur - th + 1
   if top < 1 then top = 1
   if ccol < 1 then ccol = 1
   if ccol > nc then ccol = nc
   if hcol < 1 then hcol = 1
   if hcol > ccol then hcol = ccol
   avail = w{'w'} + 0 - 2                            ;* the lead cell and the scroll bar column are not for cells
   loop
      used = 0
      for c = hcol to ccol
         used += cw<1, c> + 1
      next c
   while used - 1 > avail and hcol < ccol
      hcol += 1
   repeat
   return

store:
   w{'cur'} = cur
   w{'top'} = top
   if multi then
      w{'value'} = picked
   end else
      i = cur
      gosub orig
      w{'value'} = oi
      if cur < 1 then w{'value'} = 0
   end
   w{'ord'} = ord
   w{'fon'} = fon
   w{'nshown'} = n
   w{'picked'} = picked
   w{'ccol'} = ccol
   w{'hcol'} = hcol
   w{'sortcol'} = sortcol
   w{'sortdir'} = sortdir
   w{'cwid'} = cwid
   w{'colsel'} = colsel
   return

paint:
   tw = w{'w'} - 1                                   ;* the last column is the scroll bar
   if tw < 1 then tw = 1
   call $sl_attr('header', hc)
   call $sl_attr('text', tc)
   call $sl_attr('highlight', ac)
   call $sl_attr('scroll', wc)                  ;* 14 Oct 26: wc is only the scroll bar's column; was 'window'
   call $sl_scrollbar(th, top, n, th, sbc)
   focused = w{'focused'} + 0

   * the heading
   isdata = 0
   line = ' '
   hatr = str(hc, tw)
   if hcol < 1 then hcol = 1
   for c = hcol to nc
      cell = cols<1, c, 1>
      x0 = len(line)
      gosub fit
      if c = sortcol and sortdir > 0 then
         * the heading says how it is sorted in a blank cell of its column (the first, else the last), else over its last
         mk = if sortdir = 1 then '^' else 'v'
         begin case
            case cell[1, 1] = ' ' ; cell[1, 1] = mk
            case cell[len(cell), 1] = ' ' ; cell[len(cell), 1] = mk
            case 1 ; cell[len(cell), 1] = mk
         end case
      end
      line := cell : ' '
      if focused and c = ccol and colsel then
         for k = 1 to len(cell)
            if x0 + k <= tw then hatr[x0 + k, 1] = ac
         next k
      end
   next c
   line = line[1, tw]
   line := space(tw - len(line))
   call $sl_put(scr, w{'ax'} + 0, w{'ay'} + 0, line : ' ', hatr : wc)

   * the rows
   for r = 0 to th - 1
      i = top + r
      if i > n then
         line = space(tw)
         code = tc
      end else
         gosub orig
         lead = ' '
         if multi then
            at = 0
            if picked # '' then
               locate oi in picked<1, 1> setting at else at = 0
            end
            if at then lead = '*'
         end
         if i = cur and (not(focused) or w{'marker'} + 0) then lead = '>'     ;* marker 1: > on the current row always
         line = lead
         isdata = 1
         for c = hcol to nc
            cell = rows<oi, c>
            gosub fit
            line := cell : ' '
         next c
         line = line[1, tw]
         line := space(tw - len(line))
         code = tc
         if rowstyle # '' then
            rs = rowstyle<1, oi>
            if rs # '' then
               call $sl_attr(rs, rc)
               code = rc
            end
         end
         if i = cur and focused then code = ac
      end
      call $sl_put(scr, w{'ax'} + 0, w{'ay'} + 1 + r, line : sbc[r + 1, 1], str(code, tw) : wc)
   next r
   if focused and cur >= 1 then call $sl_curat(w{'ax'} + 0, w{'ay'} + 1 + cur - top)
   return

* cell = the text of one cell of column c, made exactly the column's width and aligned as it says
fit:
   wd = cw<1, c> + 0
   cell = convert(@sm : @tm : char(9), '...', cell)
   if isdata and ca<1, c> = 'K' then cell = (if num(cell) and cell # '' and cell + 0 # 0 then '[x]' else '[ ]')       ;* a check cell (isdata: not for the heading, fit is called for it too)
   cell = cell[1, wd]
   pad = wd - len(cell)
   begin case
      case ca<1, c> = 'R' ; cell = space(pad) : cell
      case ca<1, c> = 'C' or ca<1, c> = 'K' ; cell = space(int(pad / 2)) : cell : space(pad - int(pad / 2))
      case 1 ; cell := space(pad)
   end case
   return
end

* END-CODE
